  "question": {
    "text": "A metal surface is illuminated by a radiation of wavelength <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4500</mn><mover><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow><mo>&#8728;</mo></mover></math>. The ejected photo-electron enters a constant magnetic field of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mT</mi></math> making an angle of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>90</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> with the magnetic field. If it starts revolving in a circular path of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mm</mi></math>, the work function of the metal is approximately"
  },
